{"name":"Window Pane","hex":"#e4ecdf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"window pane","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of glass filling a window or a section of a window.","A fabric pattern of widely-spaced intersecting vertical and horizontal lines forming large squares."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/window_pane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paned window (architecture)","blocks":[{"text":"In architecture, a paned window is a window that is divided into panes of glass, usually rectangular pieces of glass that are joined to create the glazed element of the window. Window panes are often separated from other panes by lead strips, or moulded wooden strips known as glazing bars in the UK, or muntins in the US."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Window_with_recent_and_old_panes.jpg/330px-Window_with_recent_and_old_panes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paned_window_(architecture)"},{"title":"Paned window (computing)","blocks":[{"text":"A paned window is a window in a graphical user interface that has multiple parts, layers, or sections. Examples of this include a code browser in a typical integrated development environment; a file browser with multiple panels; a tiling window manager; or a web page that contains multiple frames. Simple console applications use an edit pane for accepting input and an output pane for displaying output."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Pane_window.svg/330px-Pane_window.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paned_window_(computing)"},{"title":"Window","blocks":[{"text":"A window is an opening in a wall, door, roof, or vehicle that allows the exchange of light and sometimes allows the passage of sound and air. Modern windows are usually glazed, or covered in some other transparent or translucent material, a sash set in a frame in the opening. The sash and frame are also referred to as a window. Many glazed windows may be opened, to allow ventilation, or closed to exclude inclement weather. Windows may have a latch or similar mechanism to lock the window shut or to hold it open by various amounts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Atua_Kosua_shrine4.jpg/330px-Atua_Kosua_shrine4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Mozilla-thunderbird-3.0.1.png/500px-Mozilla-thunderbird-3.0.1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Mozilla-thunderbird-3.0.1.png/500px-Mozilla-thunderbird-3.0.1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The three-paned main window of Mozilla Thunderbird.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMozilla-thunderbird-3.0.1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Window_of_the_house_with_number_17_on_strada_M%C3%A2ntuleasa%2C_from_Bucharest_%28Romania%29.jpg/500px-Window_of_the_house_with_number_17_on_strada_M%C3%A2ntuleasa%2C_from_Bucharest_%28Romania%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Window_of_the_house_with_number_17_on_strada_M%C3%A2ntuleasa%2C_from_Bucharest_%28Romania%29.jpg/1280px-Window_of_the_house_with_number_17_on_strada_M%C3%A2ntuleasa%2C_from_Bucharest_%28Romania%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Window_of_the_house_with_number_17_on_strada_M%C3%A2ntuleasa%2C_from_Bucharest_%28Romania%29.jpg/500px-Window_of_the_house_with_numbe